cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research or software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "WTI Crude Oil Volatility Research: a look-ahead-leak post-mortem and a benchmarked, reproducible next-week volatility forecaster"
authors:
  - family-names: Bawa
    given-names: Navnoor
version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-20"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/NavnoorBawa/WTI-Crude-Oil-Futures"
url: "https://navnoorbawa.github.io/WTI-Crude-Oil-Futures/"
abstract: >-
  Out-of-sample evaluation of next-week realized-volatility forecasts for front-month NYMEX WTI
  crude oil on free data: fourteen models (GARCH family, HAR family, implied volatility, gradient
  boosting, combinations) compared with QLIKE, the Model Confidence Set and Hansen's SPA test;
  weekly Value-at-Risk backtests; adaptive conformal intervals; a live, git-timestamped forward
  record; and the post-mortem of a retracted price-direction model whose backtest was a look-ahead
  leak. Every result reproduces bit for bit from a hash-pinned data snapshot.
keywords:
  - realized volatility
  - HAR model
  - implied volatility
  - model confidence set
  - value at risk
  - conformal prediction
  - look-ahead bias
  - crude oil
